---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Matt Rabah, a Detroit-based Customer Experience, Customer Success, and Implementation professional."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>

    <h1 class="display">
      I build customer lifecycle systems for operationally complex environments.
    </h1>

    <p class="lead">
      I am a Detroit-based Customer Experience, Customer Success, and
      Implementation professional with experience across healthtech, brand-side
      retail, and consulting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="background">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="background">Background</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      My background includes NeuroSync, Shinola, and Context By Design, with
      work spanning onboarding, adoption, retention, portfolio growth, CRM
      process design, and executive-facing communication.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I hold an M.S. in Customer Experience Management from Michigan State
      University’s Eli Broad College of Business, a B.S. in Organizational
      Behavior from Oakland University, and certifications across Salesforce,
      business intelligence, and inbound marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="focus">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="focus">Focus</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      My work is centered on customer lifecycle design: onboarding flows,
      account health, retention systems, CRM visibility, renewal readiness,
      stakeholder alignment, and operating cadence.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I am especially interested in healthcare, regulated, SaaS-adjacent, and
      operationally complex environments where customer success depends on clear
      ownership, consistent process, and good judgment under constraint.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>